    docs: README lanes section states the live state instead of a stale claim (CF-058)
    
    The lanes section told the reader "The scheduler also carries disabled
    code-factory-duckbrain-* rows". Measured against the live scheduler today that is
    false: six rows match ^code-factory-duckbrain and every one reports enabled=true,
    with the five duckbrain satellites nested under code-factory.
    
    The section now says what the table actually is — the family the two loaders
    configure, admission column = the loader-written default — and gives a
    copy-pasteable census command so a reader can contradict it:
    
      curl -s 'http://127.0.0.1:9090/api/v1/projects?limit=500' | jq -r ...
    
    That command prints nineteen rows on the reference deployment (the fourteen above
    plus the five duckbrain satellites this repo does not create) and surfaces the
    second drift the row names: code-factory-duckbrain reports admission=tasks while
    scripts/load_lane_config.py writes cooldown.
    
    Evidence for this change:
    - literal command re-run: 19 rows, all enabled=true, code-factory-duckbrain admission=tasks
    - bash tests/selftest.sh: SELFTEST: PASS (17 sections, README prompt/claims checks included)
    - README walk at 820e8134: every documented command reproduced the behaviour its row claims
      (lane evidence: ~/.hermes/stand-in/readme/code-factory/code-factory-readme-2026-11-03-11-27-59.md)
    
